{"id":"p10-l11","minutes":40,"summary":"A timer in PWM mode compares its counter with a capture-compare register and drives a pin from the result, and for a half-bridge it drives two complementary pins with a dead time between them so both switches are never on at once. You derive edge- and centre-aligned duty, encode a dead time into the STM32 DTG field, and test a cycle-level model of complementary outputs for duty within one count and a gap on every edge.","html":"<h2 id=\"pwm-from-a-counter\">PWM from a counter</h2>\n<p>Lesson 08’s counter runs from 0 to ARR. In <strong>PWM mode 1</strong>, output channel 1’s reference signal OC1REF is high while <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">CNT</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">CCR1</span></span></span></span></span> and low otherwise. Two counting modes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>edge-aligned</strong> (up-counting): the period is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> counts and the duty is</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.1297em;vertical-align:-0.7693em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">CCR</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7693em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">;</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>centre-aligned</strong> (up-down): the counter goes <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, the period is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span></span></span></span> counts, and the duty is</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.0463em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">CCR</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Centre-aligned PWM puts the pulse symmetrically around the counter’s valley, so the edges of the three phases of a motor drive don’t all switch at once, and the middle of the off-time (the counter peak) is a quiet moment to trigger the ADC for current sampling. It also halves the switching frequency for a given ARR: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">PWM</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"complementary-outputs-and-dead-time\">Complementary outputs and dead time</h2>\n<p>A half-bridge (lesson P09-06) has a high-side and a low-side switch. Advanced timers (TIM1, TIM8) generate CH1 and its complement CH1N from OC1REF. MOSFETs take tens to hundreds of nanoseconds to turn off, so if one switch turns on at the instant the other is told to turn off, both conduct briefly and short the supply (<strong>shoot-through</strong>). The dead-time generator delays every <em>rising</em> edge of CH1 and CH1N by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7651em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, so each output turns on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7651em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> after the other turned off. The cost is a small duty error, because during the dead time the load current flows through a diode and the bridge output depends on its direction.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"pwmdead\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Centre-aligned counter (top), OC1REF, and the complementary outputs CH1 and CH1N with the dead-time gaps shaded. Change the duty and the dead time; the DTG code updates.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"encoding-the-dead-time\">Encoding the dead time</h2>\n<p>The STM32 BDTR register’s 8-bit DTG field encodes the dead time in units of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7651em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (the timer clock period when CKD = 0) with four ranges:</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>DTG[7:5]</th>\n<th>dead time</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>0xx</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">DTG</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">7</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7651em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (0–127)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10x</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">64</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">DTG</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">])</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (128–254)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>110</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">32</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">DTG</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">])</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (256–504)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>111</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">32</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">DTG</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">:</span></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">])</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">16</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (512–1008)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>To encode a requested time, convert it to counts and pick the smallest representable value <strong>not below</strong> it: rounding down could cause shoot-through.</p>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>TIM1 at 168 MHz, 20 kHz centre-aligned PWM, 1 µs dead time, 30 % duty.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>ARR = <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">168</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4200</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>CCR = <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.30</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4200</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1260</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7651em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> = 5.952 ns, so 1 µs = 168 counts. That’s in range 2: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">64</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">168</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⇒</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span>, DTG = 0x80 | 20 = 0x94.</li>\n<li>3 µs = 504 counts, range 3: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">32</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">31</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">504</span></span></span></span>, DTG = 0xDF.</li>\n<li>CH1 is high for about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1260</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">168</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2352</span></span></span></span> counts per 8400-count period, 28.0 %. (The cycle model gives 2351: the counter visits 0 once per period, so OC1REF is high for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">CCR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> counts. That one count is within the duty tolerance.)</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">pwm_deadtime.c</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;math.h&gt;</span></span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* DTG field &lt;-&gt; dead time in t_DTS counts */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">dtg_decode</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span> d)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> ((d &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x80</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> d;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> ((d &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xC0</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x80</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">64u</span> + (d &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x3F</span>)) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2u</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> ((d &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xE0</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xC0</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">32u</span> + (d &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x1F</span>)) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">8u</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (<span class=\"hljs-number\">32u</span> + (d &amp; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x1F</span>)) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">16u</span>;\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">dtg_encode</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> counts, <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span> *out)</span> {        <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* smallest code with decode &gt;= counts */</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> best = <span class=\"hljs-number\">-1</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> bv = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFFFFFFu</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> d = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; d &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span>; d++) { <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> v = dtg_decode((<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span>)d); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (v &gt;= counts &amp;&amp; v &lt; bv) { bv = v; best = d; } }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (best &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n  *out = (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span>)best; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>;\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* cycle-level model of one centre-aligned period: counter 0..ARR..0, PWM mode 1, dead-time insertion */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> high, low_side_high, both, gaps_min, ref_high; } pwm_stats;\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> pwm_stats <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">simulate</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> arr, <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> ccr, <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> dt, <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> periods)</span> {\n  pwm_stats s = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xFFFFFFFFu</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>};\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> prev_ref = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> since_edge = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1u</span> &lt;&lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>, gap = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> ch = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, chn = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> n = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * arr;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> p = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; p &lt; periods; p++)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> t = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; t &lt; n; t++) {\n      <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> cnt = t &lt;= arr ? t : n - t;                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* up then down */</span>\n      <span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> ref = cnt &lt; ccr;\n      <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (ref != prev_ref) { since_edge = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; prev_ref = ref; } <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> since_edge++;\n      ch  = ref  &amp;&amp; since_edge &gt;= dt;                         <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* rising edges delayed by the dead time */</span>\n      chn = !ref &amp;&amp; since_edge &gt;= dt;\n      <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (p == periods - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) {                                 <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* measure the last, settled period */</span>\n        s.ref_high += ref; s.high += ch; s.low_side_high += chn; s.both += ch &amp;&amp; chn;\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (!ch &amp;&amp; !chn) gap++; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (gap) { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (gap &lt; s.gaps_min) s.gaps_min = gap; gap = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; }\n      }\n    }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> s;\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> CHECK(c) do { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (!(c)) { printf(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;FAIL line %d: %s\\n&quot;</span>, __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* the DTG encoding: every code decodes to a value that encodes back to itself */</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> d = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; d &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">256</span>; d++) { <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span> e; CHECK(dtg_encode(dtg_decode((<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span>)d), &amp;e)); CHECK(dtg_decode(e) == dtg_decode((<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span>)d)); }\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint8_t</span> code;\n  CHECK(dtg_encode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">168</span>, &amp;code) &amp;&amp; code == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0x94</span>);              <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* 1 us at 168 MHz */</span>\n  CHECK(dtg_encode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">504</span>, &amp;code) &amp;&amp; code == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0xDF</span>);              <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* 3 us */</span>\n  CHECK(dtg_encode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">129</span>, &amp;code) &amp;&amp; dtg_decode(code) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">130</span>);   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* rounds up, never down */</span>\n  CHECK(!dtg_encode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1009</span>, &amp;code));                            <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* beyond 1008 counts: needs CKD &gt; 0 */</span>\n\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> fclk = <span class=\"hljs-number\">168e6</span>, fpwm = <span class=\"hljs-number\">20e3</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> arr = (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span>)(fclk / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * fpwm));\n  CHECK(arr == <span class=\"hljs-number\">4200</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> dt = dtg_decode(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0x94</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> k = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; k &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>; k++) {\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> duty = k / <span class=\"hljs-number\">100.0</span>;\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> ccr = (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span>)lround(duty * arr);\n    pwm_stats s = simulate(arr, ccr, dt, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>);\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> measured = (<span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span>)s.ref_high / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span> * arr);\n    CHECK(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>(measured * arr - duty * arr) &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>);          <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* duty within 1 count of the command */</span>\n    CHECK(s.both == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>);                                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* never shoot-through */</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (ccr &gt; dt &amp;&amp; ccr &lt; arr - dt) CHECK(s.gaps_min &gt;= dt);  <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* a gap of at least DT on every edge */</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (k == <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>) {\n      <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;30 %%: CCR %u, OC1REF high %u, CH1 high %u (%.1f %%), CH1N high %u, min gap %u counts\\n&quot;</span>,\n             ccr, s.ref_high, s.high, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100.0</span> * s.high / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * arr), s.low_side_high, s.gaps_min);\n      CHECK(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>((<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span>)s.ref_high - <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1260</span>) &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &amp;&amp; s.high == s.ref_high - <span class=\"hljs-number\">168</span> &amp;&amp; s.gaps_min == <span class=\"hljs-number\">168</span>);\n    }\n  }\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;101 duty commands: duty within 1 count, no overlap, gaps &gt;= %u counts (%.0f ns)\\nPASS\\n&quot;</span>, dt, dt / fclk * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e9</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>At 95 % duty with 1 µs dead time at 20 kHz, how long is CH1N on per period, and why does that matter for a bootstrap gate driver?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>OC1REF is low for 5 % of 50 µs = 2.5 µs, and CH1N turns on 1 µs after that starts, so 1.5 µs per period. A bootstrap high-side supply recharges only while the low side is on; at high duty it may not get enough time, so drivers cap the maximum duty (for example 95–98 %).</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why do you round the dead time <em>up</em> when encoding?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Too little dead time lets both switches conduct during the transition, which can destroy them; too much only costs a slightly larger duty error and diode conduction losses. The safe direction is always longer.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p10-l11\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"pwm-from-a-counter","title":"PWM from a counter"},{"id":"complementary-outputs-and-dead-time","title":"Complementary outputs and dead time"},{"id":"encoding-the-dead-time","title":"Encoding the dead time"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p10-l11-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Centre-aligned PWM at 168 MHz with ARR = 4200. PWM frequency in kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f_clk / (2 ARR).</p>\n","answer":20,"tol":0.001,"unit":"kHz"},{"id":"p10-l11-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Edge-aligned with ARR = 999, CCR = 250. Duty in percent?</p>\n","explain":"<p>CCR/(ARR+1).</p>\n","answer":25,"tol":0.001,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p10-l11-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Dead time in ns for DTG = 0x94 at 168 MHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Range 2, (64+20)·2 counts.</p>\n","answer":1000,"tol":0.001,"unit":"ns"},{"id":"p10-l11-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Largest dead time in µs with CKD = 0 at 168 MHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1008 counts.</p>\n","answer":6,"tol":0.001,"unit":"µs"},{"id":"p10-l11-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>What does dead-time insertion delay?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Each output turns on late, after the other turned off.</p>\n","options":["the ADC trigger","every falling edge","the update event","every rising edge of CH1 and CH1N"],"answer":3},{"id":"p10-l11-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why is the counter peak in centre-aligned mode a good ADC trigger for current sensing?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Sample in the quiet middle.</p>\n","options":["the ADC needs it","it doubles the sample rate","it is the middle of a switching interval, away from the switching edges and their ringing","the counter is fastest there"],"answer":2}],"code":[{"file":"pwm_deadtime.c","lang":"c","src":"#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n/* DTG field <-> dead time in t_DTS counts */\nstatic uint32_t dtg_decode(uint8_t d) {\n  if ((d & 0x80) == 0)    return d;\n  if ((d & 0xC0) == 0x80) return (64u + (d & 0x3F)) * 2u;\n  if ((d & 0xE0) == 0xC0) return (32u + (d & 0x1F)) * 8u;\n  return (32u + (d & 0x1F)) * 16u;\n}\nstatic int dtg_encode(uint32_t counts, uint8_t *out) {        /* smallest code with decode >= counts */\n  int best = -1; uint32_t bv = 0xFFFFFFFFu;\n  for (int d = 0; d < 256; d++) { uint32_t v = dtg_decode((uint8_t)d); if (v >= counts && v < bv) { bv = v; best = d; } }\n  if (best < 0) return 0;\n  *out = (uint8_t)best; return 1;\n}\n\n/* cycle-level model of one centre-aligned period: counter 0..ARR..0, PWM mode 1, dead-time insertion */\ntypedef struct { uint32_t high, low_side_high, both, gaps_min, ref_high; } pwm_stats;\nstatic pwm_stats simulate(uint32_t arr, uint32_t ccr, uint32_t dt, int periods) {\n  pwm_stats s = {0, 0, 0, 0xFFFFFFFFu, 0};\n  int prev_ref = 0; uint32_t since_edge = 1u << 30, gap = 0; int ch = 0, chn = 0;\n  uint32_t n = 2 * arr;\n  for (int p = 0; p < periods; p++)\n    for (uint32_t t = 0; t < n; t++) {\n      uint32_t cnt = t <= arr ? t : n - t;                    /* up then down */\n      int ref = cnt < ccr;\n      if (ref != prev_ref) { since_edge = 0; prev_ref = ref; } else since_edge++;\n      ch  = ref  && since_edge >= dt;                         /* rising edges delayed by the dead time */\n      chn = !ref && since_edge >= dt;\n      if (p == periods - 1) {                                 /* measure the last, settled period */\n        s.ref_high += ref; s.high += ch; s.low_side_high += chn; s.both += ch && chn;\n        if (!ch && !chn) gap++; else if (gap) { if (gap < s.gaps_min) s.gaps_min = gap; gap = 0; }\n      }\n    }\n  return s;\n}\n#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { printf(\"FAIL line %d: %s\\n\", __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)\n\nint main(void) {\n  /* the DTG encoding: every code decodes to a value that encodes back to itself */\n  for (int d = 0; d < 256; d++) { uint8_t e; CHECK(dtg_encode(dtg_decode((uint8_t)d), &e)); CHECK(dtg_decode(e) == dtg_decode((uint8_t)d)); }\n  uint8_t code;\n  CHECK(dtg_encode(168, &code) && code == 0x94);              /* 1 us at 168 MHz */\n  CHECK(dtg_encode(504, &code) && code == 0xDF);              /* 3 us */\n  CHECK(dtg_encode(129, &code) && dtg_decode(code) == 130);   /* rounds up, never down */\n  CHECK(!dtg_encode(1009, &code));                            /* beyond 1008 counts: needs CKD > 0 */\n\n  const double fclk = 168e6, fpwm = 20e3;\n  uint32_t arr = (uint32_t)(fclk / (2 * fpwm));\n  CHECK(arr == 4200);\n  uint32_t dt = dtg_decode(0x94);\n  for (int k = 0; k <= 100; k++) {\n    double duty = k / 100.0;\n    uint32_t ccr = (uint32_t)lround(duty * arr);\n    pwm_stats s = simulate(arr, ccr, dt, 2);\n    double measured = (double)s.ref_high / (2.0 * arr);\n    CHECK(fabs(measured * arr - duty * arr) <= 1.0);          /* duty within 1 count of the command */\n    CHECK(s.both == 0);                                       /* never shoot-through */\n    if (ccr > dt && ccr < arr - dt) CHECK(s.gaps_min >= dt);  /* a gap of at least DT on every edge */\n    if (k == 30) {\n      printf(\"30 %%: CCR %u, OC1REF high %u, CH1 high %u (%.1f %%), CH1N high %u, min gap %u counts\\n\",\n             ccr, s.ref_high, s.high, 100.0 * s.high / (2 * arr), s.low_side_high, s.gaps_min);\n      CHECK(abs((int)s.ref_high - 2 * 1260) <= 1 && s.high == s.ref_high - 168 && s.gaps_min == 168);\n    }\n  }\n  printf(\"101 duty commands: duty within 1 count, no overlap, gaps >= %u counts (%.0f ns)\\nPASS\\n\", dt, dt / fclk * 1e9);\n  return 0;\n}"}]}